# UI Brain + MUPI Retail (virtualFit)

Use strong UI-system judgment (component hierarchy, spacing rhythm, visual consistency), but always prioritize the kiosk context below over generic web patterns.

## MUPI constraints (required)
- Target is portrait 55in MUPI, touch-first, viewing distance 1-2m.
- Keep one clear primary action per screen.
- Minimum touch target: 44px absolute minimum, prefer 56-72px on primary controls.
- Avoid desktop-like dense sidebars and tiny labels.
- Keep camera overlays outside critical face/framing zones.
- Do not introduce "desktop vs mupi" switchers in customer-facing UI.

## Studio rail rules
- Preserve readable rail width; avoid ultra-narrow panels that truncate core copy.
- Keep section typography compact and legible in rail context.
- Product tiles must remain scannable: stable image ratio, readable label (2 lines max), clear selected state.
- Category chips must fit cleanly on one row when possible and stay tappable.

## Visual quality rules
- Prefer calm, premium layout over noisy effects.
- Avoid overlapping floating elements that block primary content.
- Keep spacing and alignment mathematically consistent across sections.
- Reduce cognitive load: fewer competing CTAs, clearer hierarchy.

## Implementation habits
- Validate changes with actual MUPI-like viewport proportions before finalizing.
- If a visual change degrades readability or alignment, revert quickly and iterate with smaller deltas.
